Proposal: Full-Feature OBD2 IoT Vehicle Intelligence & Mechanic Hailing Platform
1. Introduction
This proposal outlines a comprehensive vehicle intelligence platform powered by an OBD2 IoT device (non-Bluetooth) integrated with cloud services, mobile/web applications, and an on-demand mechanic hailing system. The platform will cater to individual car users, small/large fleet operators, and professional mechanics, transforming vehicle maintenance into a predictive, connected, and seamless experience.
________________________________________
2. System Overview
The project will deliver a modular system comprising:
•	Hardware: A custom OBD2 device with SIM-enabled cellular connectivity.
•	Software: Mobile apps (drivers/fleet), web dashboards (admins/mechanics), and a real-time backend.
•	Marketplace: A service layer for locating, booking, and communicating with nearby verified mechanics.
________________________________________
3. Functionalities
A. Real-Time Diagnostics
•	Live vehicle data (RPM, speed, engine load, temperature, fuel level)
•	MIL (Check Engine Light) monitoring
•	Auto-scanning of Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs)
•	Fault code severity tagging and explanation
•	Option to clear DTCs (if safe)
B. Trip Management
•	Trip start/stop detection
•	Distance, duration, and route mapping
•	Fuel efficiency estimation
•	Driving pattern detection (e.g., aggressive acceleration/braking)
•	Trip export for reporting
C. Maintenance Management
•	Scheduled maintenance reminders
•	Service history tracking
•	Smart alerts based on usage (oil, brakes, filters)
•	Maintenance cost tracking
D. Driving Behavior Analysis
•	Harsh braking and acceleration detection
•	Overspeed alerts
•	Cornering sharpness monitoring
•	Driver score generation
•	Behavior reports for fleets
E. Vehicle Health Analytics
•	Engine, battery, transmission, fuel system condition over time
•	Historical fault tracking
•	Early warning system for potential faults
F. Emergency Mechanic Hailing
•	Fault-triggered or manual SOS mechanic request
•	Nearby mechanic auto-matching (based on fault type)
•	Real-time GPS sharing between user and mechanic
•	In-app chat and optional video call with mechanic
•	Live mechanic location tracking
•	Estimated time of arrival (ETA)
•	Ratings and feedback after service
G. Geofencing & Anti-Theft
•	Set geofence zones
•	Receive alerts when vehicle enters/exits zones
•	Remote engine immobilization (optional add-on)
•	Unauthorized movement detection
H. Vehicle Location & Tracking
•	Live GPS tracking of vehicle location
•	Breadcrumb trail of recent movement
•	History of parking locations
I. Mechanic Portal
•	Job listing based on location and fault type
•	Accept/reject job requests
•	Navigation to customer
•	Status updates (e.g., en route, job started, job done)
•	Wallet for payments and withdrawals
•	Profile, reviews, and availability toggling
J. Driver and Fleet Portals
•	Multi-vehicle support
•	Add/manage cars
•	Assign drivers
•	View trip history per driver
•	Analyze fleet performance
•	Admin assign repair approvals and follow-ups
K. Vehicle Document Vault
•	Upload and manage:
o	Insurance
o	Logbook
o	Service history
o	Roadworthiness certificate
•	Auto-expiry reminders and renewals
L. Smart Notifications
•	Service due
•	Battery low
•	Unusual driving pattern
•	DTC severity alerts
•	Mechanic en route/status updates
M. Crowdsourced Fault Solutions
•	Fault code lookups from global database
•	User-contributed resolutions and comments
•	AI-based suggestions from historical repairs
N. Voice Assistant Integration (Future Extension)
•	Voice commands for checking car status
•	Asking for trip summaries
•	Requesting a mechanic
O. Offline Caching
•	Data collection during poor network conditions
•	Automatic syncing once online
P. Admin Dashboard
•	Manage users, cars, mechanics, and subscriptions
•	View system usage and diagnostics
•	Control geofencing policies
•	Review feedback and complaints
•	Revenue monitoring and reports
________________________________________
4. Supported User Segments
User Type	Key Functions
Private Driver	Diagnostics, mechanic hailing, reminders, trip logs, document storage
Fleet Driver	Trip tracking, fault reporting, basic driving behavior
Fleet Manager	Vehicle performance overview, analytics, maintenance planning
Mechanic	Fault-specific jobs, GPS navigation, live chat/video, customer rating system
Admin	Platform control, analytics, billing, SLA monitoring
________________________________________
5. Deployment Plans
•	Mobile Apps: Android & iOS using React Native expo
•	Backend: Supabase
•	Database: Supabase/PostgreSQL for structured data, optionally MongoDB for logs
•	Hosting: Firebase/AWS/GCP
•	Device Firmware: ESP32 + SIM7600 with OBD2 parsing and secure cloud comms
________________________________________
6. Monetization & Packages
Package Type	Inclusions
Free Basic	Basic diagnostics, mechanic hailing, trip history
Pro Individual	Advanced diagnostics, driving behavior, document vault, mechanic ETA
Fleet Small	Up to 10 vehicles, dashboard, route monitoring, service history
Fleet Large	Unlimited vehicles, driver scores, alerts, enterprise API access
Mechanic Tiered Access	Lead access + job tools; pay-per-job or monthly subscription
________________________________________
7. Competitive Advantages
•	100% cellular—no Bluetooth dependency
•	Real-time mechanic matching
•	Offline caching for remote driving
•	Crowdsourced repair intelligence
•	Scalable to fleets and individual drivers
•	Locally built and customizable for African markets
________________________________________
8. Future Extensions (Post-MVP)
•	Insurance partner integration for pay-how-you-drive policies
•	AI mechanic assistant for remote diagnosis
•	Integration with national road safety authorities
•	Smart tire pressure, coolant, and battery sensor add-ons
•	Voice assistant and smart speaker support
•	Workshop repair scheduling

